Turboism __VERSION__ Windows Package - User Guide
=================================================

Turboism is a Java agent runtime that adds enhanced capabilities to the
Live2D Cubism editor. This package is a manual, admin-free installation
(ZIP): extract and run. It does not modify the Cubism installation directory.

1. Directory layout
-------------------
  turboism-agent.jar             Runtime (Java agent)
  config.json                    Runtime configuration (turboism.runtime.config v1)
  launch-cubism-turboism.bat     Launcher (double-click to run, recommended)
  launch-cubism-turboism.ps1     PowerShell version with the same logic
  plugins/                       Plugin jars (full package only; absent in lite)
  README.txt / README.zh.txt / README.ja.txt / LICENSE.txt

2. Usage
--------
1. Place the whole folder anywhere, e.g. %LOCALAPPDATA%\Turboism.
2. Double-click launch-cubism-turboism.bat to start the Cubism editor:
   - The launcher uses Cubism's bundled JDK and official classpath and
     does not modify any Cubism file;
   - It auto-detects common install paths of Live2D Cubism 5.3.02 / 5.2.03;
   - If not found, set the environment variable CUBISM_ROOT or pass the
     Cubism root on the command line:
       launch-cubism-turboism.bat -CubismRoot "C:\Program Files\Live2D Cubism 5.3.02"
3. (Optional) Set the environment variable TURBOISM_HOME to this folder; the
   launcher then works from any location (otherwise it uses its own folder
   as the Turboism home).
4. Plugin on/off: run configure_turboism.ps1 to check/uncheck plugins and
   save the result to config.json.

3. config.json
--------------
  worktreeId:       "turboism-runtime"
  pluginDirs:       ["plugins"]
  disabledPlugins:  ids of disabled plugins (unchecked ones, ascending; optional)

4. Uninstall
------------
- If you installed with the NSIS installer (TurboismInstaller-<ver>.exe),
  run uninstall.exe in the Turboism home directory. The uninstall
  confirmation page has a check box "Also delete config.json (user
  configuration)" - checked by default; uncheck it to keep config.json.
- ZIP manual installs have no uninstaller: just delete the folder.

5. FAQ
------
- The bat window closes immediately: run launch-cubism-turboism.ps1 from a
  command line to see the error.
- Plugins not working: make sure the plugin jars are under plugins/ and the
  plugin id is not listed in disabledPlugins in config.json.
- Logs: <Turboism home>\logs\runtime\YYYY-MM-DD\turboism-*.log
